# 🚩 Challenge: [Sleuthkit Apprentice]
![sleuthkit_apprentice_qn](sleuthkit_apprentice.png)
## 📝 Challenge Description
Download this disk image and find the flag.

Note: if you are using the webshell, download and extract the disk image into /tmp not your home directory.

Download compressed disk image


### Code / Terminal Snippets
```bash
1. wget https://challenge-files.cylabacademy.net/library/699d021acdedf3ce7c6944b6f3e16046a82b3a1f7ee2e79716132292ce4adbbd/disk.flag.img.gz
2. gunzip disk.flag.img.gz
3. sudo apt install sleuthkit
4. mmls disk.flag.img.gz
5. fls -h
6. fls -o 360448 disk.flag.img.gz
7. fls -o 360448 disk.flag.img.gz 1995
8. fls -o 360448 disk.flag.img.gz 3981
9. icat -o 360448 disk.flag.img.gz 2371

```

---

## 🚀 Exploitation / Solution Path
Detail your step-by-step breakdown to get the flag:

1. Download the `disk.flad.img.gz` file from challenge and extract it using `gunzip`.
2. Check the file using `file`.
3. Download `sleuthkit` if not installed before.
4. Check the `mmls disk.flag.img` and the size of the disk will be displayed.
5. Atlast one in start copy the bytes in mmmls output.
6. List the files and directory names using `fls` with specified `imgoffset` from mmls output.
7. From that again use `root inode   number`.
8. Again same command of `fls` with changing last number and keep `my_folder inode number`.
9. display the content of the image file using `icat` and place `flag.uni.txt inode number` instead of `my_folder_inode number`.
10. The flag will appear. 


